# ChemPal core rules

ChemPal is a Manifest V3 browser extension (Chrome + Firefox) that searches ~30 chemical
suppliers and normalizes prices/quantities. React 19 + MUI 7, TypeScript, Vite, pnpm.

The full guide is @AGENTS.md — read it before non-trivial work. This rule only restates what
gets missed most. Edit the source docs, not this file, when a convention changes.

## Commands

- Typecheck: `pnpm type-check` (`tsc -b`). `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json` checks nothing.
- Unit tests: `pnpm test:run` — never bare `vitest` (skips the config and the no-network guard).
- `pnpm run docs` and `pnpm run pack` need `run`; plain `pnpm docs`/`pnpm pack` are pnpm builtins.
- **Run `pnpm format` after editing** — there's no auto-format hook in Cursor. Don't hand-fix
  quotes or wrapping.
- Verify in order: `pnpm type-check` → `pnpm lint` → `pnpm test:run` → E2E if user-facing.

## Invariants

- No `as` assertions or `!` non-null assertions outside test files.
- Every function gets a TSDoc block, including private helpers. Malformed TSDoc fails lint.
- Declare all class properties at the top of the class, above the methods.
- Named imports from `react` (`import { useState } from 'react'`), never the default import.
- Logger calls are `(message, { details })`. Caught errors: name the variable `error`,
  `` logger.warn(`Failed to load: ${getErrorMessage(error)}`, { error }) ``. No trailing `:`.
- i18n changes land in all 8 locales in the same change.

## Off-limits

- `docs/` is generated TypeDoc output; `dev/` is gitignored scratch — don't read or edit either.
- Never hand-edit `src/constants/supplierMeta.generated.ts` or `public/static/images/logo/*`;
  run `pnpm run generate`.
